{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795828633,"nonce":"RYafX395dKJYggnngHeudJDVXII=","title":"CSS word-spacing is not parsed, and rich text has no letter or word spacing","message":"word-spacing has no case in blinc_css, so a stylesheet cannot set it. Text::word_spacing works (662bea6), and letter-spacing works from both.\n\nAdding the property means ElementStyle, the parser, RenderProps, inheritance (the text inheritance lives in more than one place) and the remeasure after a restyle, following letter-spacing.\n\nRichText has no letter_spacing or word_spacing modifier, and its box is measured without letter spacing. A CSS letter-spacing on a rich text still reaches each drawn segment, while the segment positions and the line wrapping are measured without it, so segments can overlap. This is from reading the code in node_content (the StyledText branch); it has no reproducer yet.","files":null}]}